pplication-level failures (e.g., database connection issues, invalid configuration). This is critical to pinpoint the exact reason for the crash.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 397, 'prompt_tokens': 3957, 'total_tokens': 4354, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb48-fcba-7a32-815c-15cec53cb247-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3957, 'output_tokens': 397, 'total_tokens': 4354}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='17d8d7ee-3c66-4ff3-9c33-eeeb3389b39d'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose why the 'rate' deployment isn't working. The deployment has a pod in CrashLoopBackOff, which means it's crashing repeatedly. The previous steps have already checked the deployments, pods, and described the deployment, but the issue persists.\n\nThe next logical step is to check the logs of the crashing pod. The command `kubectl logs` would retrieve the logs for the specific pod, which can show any errors or exceptions that occur when the container starts or runs. Since the pod is in CrashLoopBackOff, the logs should indicate why the container is failing. Possible issues could be application errors, missing files, incorrect environment variables, or problems connecting to other services like databases.\n\nThe user has the necessary tool `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` to run the command. The correct command would be `kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-rqdhz -n hotel-reservation`. This will fetch the logs for the specific pod, allowing the user to see the exact error messages and determine the root cause. Once the logs are obtained, they can analyze the output to find the problem, such as a configuration mistake or a dependency issue. Then, based on the logs, further actions can be taken, like fixing the configuration or checking service availability.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-rqdhz -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-81cdc8a87e6bb33d', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 317, 'prompt_tokens': 4996, 'total_tokens': 5313, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb49-0f7a-79d3-a83d-7e51133a0c68-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-rqdhz -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-81cdc8a87e6bb33d', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4996, 'output_tokens': 317, 'total_tokens': 5313}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T10:13:03Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T10:13:03Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T10:13:03Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T10:13:03Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/rate/main.go:24\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T10:13:03Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/rate/main.go:37\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead database URL: mongodb-rate:27017\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T10:13:03Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/rate/main.go:38\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing DB connection...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T10:13:03Z\x1b[0m \x1b[31mPNC\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/rate/db.go:36\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[