atively, maybe check the metrics for each service to see if there are any anomalies. But without knowing which service is faulty, it\'s better to first list all the services and their deployments and pods. \n\nSo the next step after getting the services is to get deployments and then pods. But the user\'s previous step was to get services. Now, the next tool call should be to get deployments. So the command would be "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation". \n\nBut the user might also need to check the pods for each service. However, the available commands include "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation". \n\nAlternatively, maybe check the metrics for each service to see if there are any errors. But the user hasn\'t done that yet. \n\nSo, the next logical step is to get deployments to check their status. If deployments are not healthy, that could indicate the root cause. Then, check the pods for any issues. \n\nTherefore, the next tool call should be to get deployments using "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation".\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8f72a45dee4cb991', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 747, 'prompt_tokens': 2523, 'total_tokens': 3270, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb48-5b62-7082-a587-6b9f96a09f64-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8f72a45dee4cb991', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2523, 'output_tokens': 747, 'total_tokens': 3270}), ToolMessage(